[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: The creator introduces the weekly update on Gaussian splatting.
AUDIO: 'I\'ve been covering radiance field for nearly 5 years now. Last week was one of those weeks where it feels like everything is beginning to shift. We saw it releases from Play Canvas Super Splat with 3JS formally added Gaussian Splatting support and world labs pushed another major update to Spark. And this'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'week at Intergeo, we\'re going to be seeing multiple camera companies launching new hardware specific for Gaussian Splatting. For Aussie, the part that I\'m most excited about is 4D Gaussian Splatting because it\'s starting to feel like to me it\'s an NGP back in'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '2022 where we\'re starting to see people really begin to figure out where this technology is headed and how to build with it. There\'s a ton to get through this week.'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, let\'s start with the web because that\'s where the most activity happened this last week. The really big story this week was Play Canvas launching Super Splat 3.0, which is the first major update since Super Splat released 2.0 back in February of 2025. And with'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this 3.0 comes a whole bunch of really incredible features and enhancements. One of them is the addition of global sorting, which dramatically helps render stability on the web, especially with captures with higher splat counts. And'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'captures that used to struggle on my phone now render so much smoother. Super Splat 3.0 also completes the move to web GPU, meaning that you will need to use a browser that has web GPU enabled. If you\'re sitting there wondering what web GPU is, here some of the browsers that'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are you don\'t even have to think about. If you\'re on Chrome, Edge, Safari 26, you\'re totally fine. If you\'re using Firefox like me, you just have to enable the flags where web GPU to use it. I\'m actually creating a much more detailed tutorial on how to use Super Splat'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'end-to-end in the coming days too. So, please be on the lookout for that. If you\'re interested, definitely subscribe. But, this wasn\'t even the most consequential announcement for Gaussian Splatting on the web last week. We also saw the formal integration of Gaussian Splatting right into 3JS in the release'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of 186 for 3JS. 3JS, which is one of the most popular web frameworks on the entire internet, just supported Gaussian Splatting natively for the first time. Splat efficient autos might recognize'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that this isn\'t the first time we\'ve had 3JS support with Gaussian splatting. OG fans of splats will realize that there is a course Mark Kellogg\'s Gaussian splats 3 which brought the case flat file format. Last week we saw a ton of activity from the world labs team inside'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of spark. The 2.2 version speeds up level of detail changing and also takes more advantage of rust as a library. And speaking of world labs, I\'ve heard that Atlas will begin rolling out early access this week to a small group of'

